{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1526579-the-last-nights-of-the-caliphate","id":1526579,"title":"The Last Nights of the Caliphate","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-12-09T20:06:45-08:00","id":1526579,"title":"The Last Nights of the Caliphate","content":"<img width=\"140\" height=\"181\" data-align=\"left\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://d1vzi28wh99zvq.cloudfront.net/images/1/463265-thumb140.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://d1vzi28wh99zvq.cloudfront.net/images/1/463265-thumb140.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://d1vzi28wh99zvq.cloudfront.net/images/1/463265-thumb140.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_left js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <b>The Jewel of the Islamic World</b><br /> In the heart of the Islamic world, where the golden threads of history are woven with tales of mystique and grandeur, there exists a city that defied the very essence of time\u2014Baghdad, the Jewel of the East. Nestled on the banks of the Tigris River, the city is known for its opulent palaces, housing the Caliph, his family and advisors, and the most powerful lords of the empire. Resplendent jewels, they stand as testament to architectural brilliance, adorned with mosaics telling the stories of Scheherazade's fables. This is a city of private estates and pleasure gardens, sanctuaries where poets seek inspiration under the shade of date palms, and courtesans spin tales of love that echo through the marble halls. The soothing melody of fountains and the gentle rustle of leaves paint a symphony that serenaded the city beneath the watchful gaze of a thousand stars.<br /> <br /> As the sun dips below the horizon, Baghdad awakes from its daytime slumber to unveil a nocturnal enchantment. Lantern-lit bazaars come alive, a bustling kaleidoscope of silks, spices, and secrets. The scent of cardamom and incense hang in the air like a fragrant spell, weaving through narrow alleyways that whispered ancient tales to those who traversed them.<br /> <br /> Yet, amidst the splendour, shadows lurk in the alleyways of Baghdad. Cloaked figures move like phantoms through the labyrinthine streets, exchanging coded whispers that echo the clandestine affairs of the city's political machinations. There are threats which hide in the shadows of the City of Peace, and one would be foolish to underestimate the dangers which lie lurking in the night.<br /> <br /> <b>The Last Nights of the Caliphate includes:</b><ul><li>An overview of Baghdad, heart of the Abbasid Caliphate, including extensive material on the metropolis of Baghdad.</li> <li>Profiles of 120 characters, describing the Cainites residing in the greatest of all medieval cities.</li> <li>Information on the secrets of the Web of Knives, a conspiracy amongst the Children of Haqim which threatens to transform the world of Cainites.</li> <li>Maps, timelines, and other reference material designed to support chronicles set at the heart of the Islamic world.\u200b</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-09T20:25:09-08:00","id":1526580,"title":"","content":"Oh,this looks cool!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-09T20:58:09-08:00","id":1526581,"title":"","content":"And, I cannot believe, I missed out the link:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/463265/The-Last-Nights-of-the-Caliphate?src=newest_community&amp;filters=45622_45629\" target=\"_blank\">The Last Nights of the Caliphate on Storyteller's Vault</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-10T13:28:32-08:00","id":1526624,"title":"","content":"Given the title, does the book address anything as far as, how to put it, A Surprise Hulagu Approaches!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-10T17:40:37-08:00","id":1526642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1526579-the-last-nights-of-the-caliphate?p=1526624#post1526624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given the title, does the book address anything as far as, how to put it, A Surprise Hulagu Approaches!</div> </div> </div> </div>The Caliph is, at least on paper, one of the richest and most powerful men in the world, with a large army at his disposal, and the support of many of the rulers of the Islamic world; what chance would some nomads from Central Asia have against the forces at his disposal?<br /> <br /> And there's only one Anda resident amongst the Cainites of Baghdad. Nothing remotely ominous there...<br /> <br /> (It's worth noting that the contents page and entire introduction is available as the preview on the Storyteller's Vault, which will give the reader a bit of an idea of what is going on.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-10T20:05:45-08:00","id":1526648,"title":"","content":"Very cool! I always look forward to your books showing up on Storyteller's Vault. You create, by far, the best 3rd-party RPG material I've purchased, and the breadth of your published subject material is impressive. I'm often not entirely satisfied with the 3rd-party Vampire products I buy on Storyteller's Vault as I'm quite picky when it comes to art, layout and editing, but your work is always top shelf and I've never regretted picking up one of your books.<br /> <br /> I would say that England Will Burn rivals Constantinople by Night for one of the best (and most useful) VtDA books, and it became my go-to sourcebook for running a game in Chester. Thank you for your continued dedication to releasing high-quality material for Vampire: the Dark Ages, it is much appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27237,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27237-snikabar","user":"Snikabar","date":". 12-10-2023, 11:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27237-snikabar","name":"Snikabar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-12T00:08:23-08:00","id":1526693,"title":"","content":"I have been intending to add a few chapters to <i>England Will Burn</i>; Norwich and Coventry would come next, as well as an across-the-board visual uplift. <br /> <br /> I should do a poll on what book to write next; there are a few ideas under consideration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-12T16:43:58-08:00","id":1526722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>James_Willoughby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1526579-the-last-nights-of-the-caliphate?p=1526693#post1526693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I should do a poll on what book to write next; there are a few ideas under consideration.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have always thought that Paris and Venice would have made great Dark Ages by Night books, 'though medieval Burgandy and Naples also have a lot to play around with.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-12T17:45:43-08:00","id":1526725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1526579-the-last-nights-of-the-caliphate?p=1526722#post1526722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have always thought that Paris and Venice would have made great Dark Ages by Night books, 'though medieval Burgandy and Naples also have a lot to play around with.</div> </div> </div> </div>These are excellent suggestions.<br /> <br /> Somewhere in France would be great, but especially Paris as the Toreador have established vampiric connections/tensions with England as described in Legacy of Lies (notably the rivalry between Marcus Verus and Robert Durand). England Will Burn and a Paris by Night book would make a great pair of sourcebooks for Cainites with ties to either the court of Mithras or Salianna.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, I think Venice is a natural fit for backstabbing politics, secret societies and intrigue. It has the wealth and sophistication to make courtly roleplaying the center of a chronicle, but its position as major trade hub between Western Europe and the Middle East allows for all kinds of adventures and character/clan options.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27237-snikabar","name":"Snikabar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-12T22:59:48-08:00","id":1526732,"title":"","content":"France by Night would need maybe 300 to 320 pages. 120-130 for Paris, another 100 for Rouen (and, given that Rouen is the capital of Normandy, and a key link between the Kingdoms of England and France you would really want to detail the city), then at least one other location, preferably in the Midi (Carcassone? Montpellier?). Add a chapter for geography, appendices, and all the rest, and you would have a fairly substantial book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-13T00:14:19-08:00","id":1526733,"title":"","content":"Medieval France is such a diverse and complicated place. I've long been annoyed at how hard it has been to find a layman's history of France that doesn't just focus on Paris and the areas it actually had control over.<br /> <br /> If I ever start my Ages of Darkness thread back up, I may try to talk about Brittany as a setting for DA Mage and Fae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-13T08:14:38-08:00","id":1526755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>James_Willoughby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1526579-the-last-nights-of-the-caliphate?p=1526732#post1526732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">France by Night would need maybe 300 to 320 pages. 120-130 for Paris, another 100 for Rouen (and, given that Rouen is the capital of Normandy, and a key link between the Kingdoms of England and France you would really want to detail the city), then at least one other location, preferably in the Midi (Carcassone? Montpellier?). Add a chapter for geography, appendices, and all the rest, and you would have a fairly substantial book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Any Cathar stronghold would make for a good backdrop to a Dark Mediaeval book; I think you could get some interesting dynamics from the divergence of opinion among vampires on the merits and usefulness of the sect. Do note the Cainite heresy is contemporaneous with the height of the Cathar movement in the Rhineland and Cologne in particular, iirc (mid-12th century); besides, I don't think we ever got an elaboration on the exact relationship between Catharism and the Path of the Cathari.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28177-gamiem","name":"gamiem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28177_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-13T20:55:15-08:00","id":1526792,"title":"","content":"Speaking of the Cathars I would mention that adding Occitania into a France by Night book or running it as a stand alone work would also be a question. Occitania has alot to offer and really isn't just &quot;a part&quot; of France to my knowledge during much of the Middle Ages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-13T21:19:26-08:00","id":1526793,"title":"","content":"France by Night being three separate books because France was so fractured in the time period feels very on point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-15T02:21:47-08:00","id":1526840,"title":"","content":"Yes, like Normandy+possible other &quot;English&quot; possessions on the Continent, Occitania and France &quot;proper&quot; might be a division that would make some sense, At least to me who is not a medievalist but has some interest in the period.<br /> <br /> And possibly running Bretange as a separate book as that remained mostly independent until 1488 unless I've gotten things wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-18T00:43:22-08:00","id":1527040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> France by Night would need maybe 300 to 320 pages </div> </div> </div>It used only 256:<br /> <a href=\"http://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/France_by_Night\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/France_by_Night</a><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28299-jjorda","name":"jjorda","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28299_1.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-18T02:57:07-08:00","id":1527042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jjorda</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1526579-the-last-nights-of-the-caliphate?p=1527040#post1527040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It used only 256:<br /> <a href=\"http://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/France_by_Night\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/France_by_Night</a></div> </div> </div> </div>No, I mean to do it properly as a Storyteller's Vault product; the Arkhane Asylum <i>France by Night</i> book has Paris described in six pages, Rouen in five. It has 42 characters, spread throughout France and the surrounding countries. It's a nice looking book (I own a copy), but not a great game resource, as it spreads itself too thin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-18T03:10:58-08:00","id":1527043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1526579-the-last-nights-of-the-caliphate?p=1526840#post1526840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, like Normandy+possible other &quot;English&quot; possessions on the Continent, Occitania and France &quot;proper&quot; might be a division that would make some sense, At least to me who is not a medievalist but has some interest in the period.<br /> <br /> And possibly running Bretange as a separate book as that remained mostly independent until 1488 unless I've gotten things wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Possessions of the English crown are Gascony and the Channel Islands, with not much in between. Brittany is not part of the Kingdom of France, but the County of Barcelona legally is (though the authority of the French king over that region only exists on paper, and is formally abolished in 1258). <br /> <br /> Realistically ... you have to think about what works thematically and commercially. From a thematic viewpoint, there's no right answer, as it would depend on what the author might want to emphasise. You could put stress on the cultural and political independence of the County of Toulouse, for instance, and create <i>Toulouse by Night</i> as a single volume, focusing on Occitan culture, Catharism, and the links to the Mediterranean world, as distinct from a <i>France by Night</i> focused on Paris, and the cultural world which has developed out of the Frankish realm. Alternately, it would be equally valid to create a single book, focused on the evolution of France as a distinct country. <br /> <br /> Commercially, however, I would rather go with a single book. People are going to want Paris by Night, and Paris, Rouen, and these cities, alongside the connections and conflict with the Kingdom of England to the north, probably make the strongest selling point for a particular volume. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-18T03:35:56-08:00","id":1527044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>James_Willoughby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1526579-the-last-nights-of-the-caliphate?p=1527043#post1527043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Possessions of the English crown are Gascony and the Channel Islands, with not much in between. Brittany is not part of the Kingdom of France, but the County of Barcelona legally is (though the authority of the French king over that region only exists on paper, and is formally abolished in 1258).<br /> <br /> Realistically ... you have to think about what works thematically and commercially. From a thematic viewpoint, there's no right answer, as it would depend on what the author might want to emphasise. You could put stress on the cultural and political independence of the County of Toulouse, for instance, and create <i>Toulouse by Night</i> as a single volume, focusing on Occitan culture, Catharism, and the links to the Mediterranean world, as distinct from a <i>France by Night</i> focused on Paris, and the cultural world which has developed out of the Frankish realm. Alternately, it would be equally valid to create a single book, focused on the evolution of France as a distinct country.<br /> <br /> Commercially, however, I would rather go with a single book. People are going to want Paris by Night, and Paris, Rouen, and these cities, alongside the connections and conflict with the Kingdom of England to the north, probably make the strongest selling point for a particular volume.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u0130 just noticed this, but &quot;By Night&quot; books seem to generally be city- rather than country- based, like Chicago or Cairo By Night.<br /> \u0130'm \u0130talian. \u0130 would find it mildly offensive if the complexity of my country was reduced to a superficial &quot;\u0130taly By Night&quot; instead of acknowledging the obvious complexity by publishing Rome/Venice/Florence etc. By Night.<br /> And \u0130'm not saying there has to be a book for each major city: one for one major city is enough. The important thing is not to reduce a whole country to a single book when cities have already received their own books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-18T14:29:18-08:00","id":1527066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1526579-the-last-nights-of-the-caliphate?p=1527044#post1527044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u0130 just noticed this, but &quot;By Night&quot; books seem to generally be city- rather than country- based, like Chicago or Cairo By Night.<br /> \u0130'm \u0130talian. \u0130 would find it mildly offensive if the complexity of my country was reduced to a superficial &quot;\u0130taly By Night&quot; instead of acknowledging the obvious complexity by publishing Rome/Venice/Florence etc. By Night.<br /> And \u0130'm not saying there has to be a book for each major city: one for one major city is enough. The important thing is not to reduce a whole country to a single book when cities have already received their own books.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampire the Dark Ages did some regional books like Transylvania by Night and Iberia by Night, and then some others like Veil of Night about the middle east broadly, Dark Ages: Europe, and Dark Ages: British Isles. I think people are just riffing on the 'By Night' titles. Dark Ages as a line has a lot more broad regional sourcebooks than city sourcebooks (Dark Ages only did city sourcebooks for Constantinople and Jerusalem)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-18T15:24:50-08:00","id":1527068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>literatzi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1526579-the-last-nights-of-the-caliphate?p=1527066#post1527066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Vampire the Dark Ages did some regional books like Transylvania by Night and Iberia by Night, and then some others like Veil of Night about the middle east broadly, Dark Ages: Europe, and Dark Ages: British Isles. I think people are just riffing on the 'By Night' titles. Dark Ages as a line has a lot more broad regional sourcebooks than city sourcebooks (Dark Ages only did city sourcebooks for Constantinople and Jerusalem)</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, you're right. \u0130 stand corrected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}